    "prompt": "The ColumnTransformer.set_output method currently ignores the remainder parameter when it is provided as an estimator. This results in the final output being incorrectly aggregated because the output setting is applied only to the designated sub-transformers and not to the remainder. The fix must ensure that the remainder transformer is treated the same as the other transformers by applying the output transformation logic. After the change, using set_output with transform='pandas' or other modes should correctly set the output for all transformer components including the remainder.",
    "hint_texts": "Implement the necessary changes in the set_output method within the sklearn/compose/_column_transformer.py file. After calling super().set_output(transform=transform), iterate through the transformers and then add a condition to check if self.remainder is not either 'passthrough' or 'drop'. If it is an estimator, call _safe_set_output on self.remainder with the given transform parameter. This change should mirror the handling of the other sub-transformers to ensure consistency.",
    "entrypoint": "File: sklearn/compose/_column_transformer.py, Method: ColumnTransformer.set_output. Focus on the code block starting around line 293 where super().set_output is called, and insert the new condition to apply _safe_set_output on self.remainder when necessary.",
